 "notes": [
  "The Department of Earth and Planetary Science offers one undergraduate major with 6 specializations:\n- Atmospheric Science\n- Geophysics\n- Environmental Earth Science\n- Marine Science\n- Geology\n- Planetary Science\nAll majors in Earth and Planetary Science take a common set of classes that provide an overview of the Earth system. EPS majors then build on this foundation by taking additional classes in a discipline specialization of their choosing.\nRequirements for each specialization are listed below the core requirements.",
  "Double Specializations\nEPS majors have the opportunity to complete up to two specializations. The opportunity to pursue more than one specialization can allow some students to explore multiple facets of the discipline and offer the ability to optimize their undergraduate learning experience, which could better inform a focus for graduate education or job placement.\nStudents who wish to complete a double specialization within the EPS major must fill out a program plan to demonstrate timely progress to complete the major by their assigned EGT. This form will be reviewed and approved by the undergraduate major advisor before adding an additional specialization. Faculty advisors will have full discretion to review proposed double specializations and to require modifications if overlapping coursework does not result in a sufficiently distinct program. No double specialization will be approved without the sign-off of the relevant faculty advisors, who will verify that the combination represents a coherent and academically meaningful course of study.\nPlease contact an EPS advisor to discuss program planning and other questions."
 ],
